<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fujiwara no Hidehira</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1122–1187</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fujiwara no Hidehira was the third lord of the Northern Fujiwara, ruling Mutsu and Dewa from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hiraizumi">Hiraizumi</a> at the height of the family's wealth. The court made him commander of the northern frontier (chinjufu-shōgun) in 1170. He sheltered the young <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minamoto-no-yoshitsune">Minamoto no Yoshitsune</a> and took him in again in 1187 as a fugitive from his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minamoto-no-yoritomo">Yoritomo</a>, shortly before Hidehira's own death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fujiwara-no-hidehira.jpg" alt="Fujiwara no Hidehira" width="320" height="291" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fujiwara_no_Hidehira.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
